{
  "question": "How do I make my API docs show an example request body?",
  "k": 5
}

Declare `examples` for your request body, and FastAPI adds them to the JSON Schema shown in the `/docs` UI. Source: https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/schema-extra-example/

**Option 1: In the Pydantic model.** You can declare `examples` for a Pydantic model that will be added to the generated JSON Schema.[3]

```python
class Item(BaseModel):
    name: str
    description: str | None = None
    price: float
    tax: float | None = None

    model_config = {
        "json_schema_extra": {
            "examples": [
                {
                    "name": "Foo",
                    "description": "A very nice Item",
                    "price": 35.4,
                    "tax": 3.2,
                }
            ]
        }
    }
```

That extra info will be added as-is to the output **JSON Schema** for that model, and it will be used in the API docs.[3]

**Option 2: Per field.** When using `Field()` with Pydantic models, you can also declare additional `examples`[1], for example `name: str = Field(examples=["Foo"])`.

**Option 3: In `Body()`.** Pass `examples` directly in the endpoint:

```python
@app.put("/items/{item_id}")
async def update_item(
    item_id: int,
    item: Annotated[
        Item,
        Body(
            examples=[
                {
                    "name": "Foo",
                    "description": "A very nice Item",
                    "price": 35.4,
                    "tax": 3.2,
                }
            ],
        ),
    ],
):
    results = {"item_id": item_id, "item": item}
    return results
```

**Multiple examples:** You can pass several examples in the `Body()` list. However, at the time of writing this, Swagger UI, the tool in charge of showing the docs UI, doesn't support showing multiple examples for the data in **JSON Schema**.[2] The docs describe a workaround that uses `openapi_examples` in `Body()`. The excerpts I found don't include its full code, so see the same page for details.

**Note:** Use `examples`, not `example`. `example` is still supported by OpenAPI 3.1.0, but is deprecated and is not part of the JSON Schema standard.[3]
